---
import MathLayout from '../../../layouts/MathLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../../utils/path';

const lang = 'en';
const currentPath = '/en/university/set-theory';
const title = 'Set Theory';
---

<MathLayout {title} {lang} {currentPath}>
	<article>
		<h1>{title}</h1>
		<p class="intro">Set theory is the foundational language of modern mathematics. It provides a unified framework for the entire mathematical world.</p>

		<h2>Core Concepts</h2>
		<div class="concepts-grid">
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>∅ Empty Set</h3>
				<p>The purest "monad", containing no elements. It is the starting point of the entire mathematical universe.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>∈ Membership</h3>
				<p>The fundamental relation between elements and sets. $a \in A$ means $a$ is an element of set $A$.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>⊆ Subsets</h3>
				<p>The inclusion relation. $A \subseteq B$ means every element of $A$ is in $B$.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="concept-card card">
				<h3>∪ ∩ Operations</h3>
				<p>Union and intersection - the basic algebraic operations on sets.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Learning Path</h2>
		<div class="learning-path">
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">1</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Basic Concepts</h3>
					<p>Sets, subsets, membership, set operations (union, intersection, complement)</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">2</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Relations & Functions</h3>
					<p>Cartesian product, binary relations, equivalence relations, partial orders, functions</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">3</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Mapping Foundations</h3>
					<p>Injective, surjective, bijective; cardinality of sets</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="path-step">
				<span class="step-num">4</span>
				<div class="step-content">
					<h3>Axiomatic Set Theory</h3>
					<p>ZFC axioms, Axiom of Choice and equivalent statements</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<h2>Connections to Other Fields</h2>
		<div class="connections">
			<div class="connection-item">
				<span class="conn-icon">⟷</span>
				<span>Mathematical Logic - Sets provide semantic foundations for proofs</span>
			</div>
			<div class="connection-item">
				<span class="conn-icon">⟷</span>
				<span>Number Theory - Natural numbers defined within set theory</span>
			</div>
			<div class="connection-item">
				<span class="conn-icon">⟷</span>
				<span>Topology - Open sets are special families of subsets</span>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="nav-footer">
			<a href={getPath('/en/university')} class="back-link">← Back to University Math</a>
		</div>
	</article>
</MathLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.concepts-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.concept-card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}

	.concept-card p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.learning-path {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.path-step {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.path-step:last-child {
		border-bottom: none;
	}

	.step-num {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 2rem;
		height: 2rem;
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6366f1, #8b5cf6);
		border-radius: 50%;
		font-weight: bold;
		font-size: 1rem;
	}

	.step-content h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
		color: #f1f5f9;
	}

	.step-content p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.connections {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.connection-item {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 0.75rem;
		background: rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.05);
		border-radius: 8px;
	}

	.conn-icon {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		color: #ec4899;
	}

	.nav-footer {
		margin-top: 3rem;
		padding-top: 2rem;
		border-top: 1px solid rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.2);
	}

	.back-link {
		color: #6366f1;
	}
</style>
